      "id": "Real.log",
      "generated_kind": null,
      "external": true,
      "docstring": "The real logarithm function, equal to the inverse of the exponential for `x > 0`,\nto `log |x|` for `x < 0`, and to `0` for `0`. We use this unconventional extension to\n`(-∞, 0]` as it gives the formula `log (x * y) = log x + log y` for all nonzero `x` and `y`, and\nthe derivative of `log` is `1/x` away from `0`. "
    },
    {
